# Backport of upstream PR #135 (commit 27a0e37, released in calrs v1.14.0+)
# onto the pinned v1.6.0 tag.
#
# Radicale (our calendar-radicale store) emits the calendar resourcetype as
# `<C:calendar />` — WITH a space before the self-closing slash. calrs v1.6.0's
# `parse_calendar_list` used a brittle substring match (`contains("calendar/>")`
# or `contains("<calendar xmlns=")`), so PROPFIND depth:1 against Radicale
# parsed calendar_count=0: no calendars were discovered, sync fetched nothing,
# and CalDAV write-back had no target collection. Replace it with
# has_calendar_resourcetype(), which matches a `calendar` resourcetype element
# under any (or no) prefix, self-closing or open, with or without the space,
# while rejecting lookalikes (calendar-color, calendar-data,
# supported-calendar-component-set) and addressbook collections.
#
# Apply AFTER 0001-oidc-zitadel-compat.patch on the v1.6.0 checkout.
commit 27a0e37d639a23c99cce95726a6af89e80f9af02
Author: Olivier Lambert <olivier.lambert@vates.tech>
Date:   Tue Jun 9 22:25:04 2026 +0200

    fix(caldav): detect Radicale calendars with spaced self-closing tag (#132) (#135)
    
    Radicale emits the calendar resourcetype as `<C:calendar />` with a space
    before the self-closing slash. The previous detection used a brittle
    substring match (`contains("calendar/>")`) that required no space, so
    PROPFIND depth:1 against Radicale parsed calendar_count=0 and no events
    were ever synced.
    
    Replace the substring check with has_calendar_resourcetype(), which
    matches a `calendar` resourcetype element under any (or no) namespace
    prefix, self-closing or open, with or without the space, while rejecting
    lookalikes (calendar-color, calendar-data, supported-calendar-
    component-set) and addressbook collections.
    
    Verified against a live Radicale 3.7.3 instance. Adds a regression test
    built from the reporter's XML plus unit coverage for the lookalikes.
    
    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

